# Two Vercel projects deploy from this repo: avatars-api (rootDirectory=backend)
# and avatar-admin (rootDirectory=admin). This file is applied to BOTH the CLI
# upload from the repo root AND to GitHub-triggered builds — Vercel reads the
# repository-root .vercelignore before honouring rootDirectory ("Found
# .vercelignore (repository root) … Removed 701 ignored files", 2026-09-04),
# so anything excluded here is simply gone for git deploys too. On 2026-09-04
# `/*` + `!/backend` made the avatar-admin git deploy of `main` ship an empty
# Next app (admin.aaavatar.nl → 404, /v1/effects → 0 items) until a rollback.
# Keep both project roots; exclude the macOS sources so the CLI upload from
# the repo root stays small.
/*
!/backend
!/admin
